Currently, you can actually get OSF DCE from DEC and Gradient Technology
as far as I am aware.  (Could have missed someone)  DEC is shipping a
developers' kit for OSF/1.  Gradient has done DCE for MS-Windows.
HP and IBM have both announced it for their Unix variants.  IBM is
supposed to have the RS/6000 version out in December, 92 and HP in early
'93.  In addition, IBM has made at least a Statement of Direction for
DCE on MVS.  (SOD ~= 18 months from the time of the statement - say late '93)

>BTW, am I right in thinking that OSF is some secret society?  I bike
>by their place all the time in Cambridge -- and strangely I never hear
>of them doing anything except in the pages of ComputerWorld and PC
>Week and the Burton Group.  Nor is there a great abundance of postings
>in comp.unix.osf.  Do I have to be on some mailing list?
