If your university is an OSF member (don't have the list handy) you can
probably get on a LOT of mailing lists.  OSF has a bunch of SIG's, for
OSF/1, Motif, DCE, DME, etc.  They generate a bunch of mail.  Getting on
the mailing list takes one of the official OSF members being on the list and
him/her moving the mail to you as it arrives.

I represent the DEC users' group, DECUS, to OSF.  I've been maintaining
a mailing list for some DECUS folks who are interested in OSF materials
but am going to start putting things onto our DECUS conferencing system
that are appropriate shortly.  The system is called DECUServe, which you
can join for a nominal fee.

Other than that, you can expect more traffic on this list, including an
FAQ as soon as I can get it together.  I'm on the End User Forum Steering
Committee of OSF and just committed to doing more on this list.

>Thanks.
